                                "sense_id": "38a9a8a4-5bcd-3bc6-ab47-9957787bcd52",
                                "text": "Anthology of Music and Dance of the Americas, The JVC/Smithsonian Folkways, Vol 1, Canada and the United States: Secular Traditions.\nEspecially welcome in this survey are two examples of turlute, or lilting. In communities where musical instruments were not available, turlute was a common dance accompaniment. The popularity and availability of musical instruments has made lilting a rare art."
